      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "The target integer must be more than $11^0=1$ since it is positive, and at least a $3^6$ since $\\color{red}{36}<3^3=27$ is the first power less than 11.\nBy trying units digits 6 and 9, the only possible candidates are the palindromes $11^6=89\\color{red}{89}\\color{red}{89}$ and $11^5=1\\color{red}{6161}$. 116161 is not divisible by any power of 2 (except by 2 itself), so $11^5$ is a possible answer, but 898989 is not divisible by any power of 5. (That is, 311981 is the smallest palindromic number that is also divisible by 5, 7, 9, 25, and 49)}.\nThe smallest such number is $\\boxed{11^5=161051}$.Answer Choices:  A. 153833  B. 115383  C. 3838981  D. 115281  E. 898989\nE\n$\\boxed{E}$",
